'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-so80-getxacc-clear-gating.spin2
''   Purpose.... SO80: does GETXACC's clear reach the Goertzel accumulators
''               only while the streamer runs in DDS/Goertzel mode (Half A),
''               and even then leave the one held term behind instead of a
''               true zero (Half B)?
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 25 Sep 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ THE PREDICTION UNDER TEST (brief BRIEF-SO80, read off the HDL, never observed
  on a part):
    Half A  With the streamer idle, or running in any mode other than
            DDS/Goertzel, GETXACC does NOT clear X/Y. The accumulators are
            frozen: repeat idle reads return bit-identical values.
    Half B  With a Goertzel burst running, GETXACC returns the running sum and
            leaves xsum = the one term xterm holds on that clock (the "held
            term"), not zero. Readings taken during one burst therefore add up
            to exactly what one read at its end returns.

  WHAT WOULD SHOW IT WRONG (written before the run, encoded in judge()):
    Half A  any idle/non-Goertzel read G differs from the preamble's B.
            G = 0 (dG = -B) specifically means the clear reached xsum.
    Half B  dd = dB - dA nonzero:  dd = R1  -> clear did not reach xsum while
            running;  dd = -C -> true zero, held term lost;  dd = +C -> held
            term counted twice;  other whole multiple of C -> refuted, other.
            dd not a whole multiple of C -> construction failed: INCONCLUSIVE.

  RIG
    P2 Edge (or any P2), NO JUMPER, nothing connected to P0..P7.
    The engine cog drives P3 (pin 4g+3, g = 0) itself as a PLAIN output, low,
    with its WRPIN config at 0 (smart pin off, A input = this pin's own read
    state). With the smart pin off, IN carries the pin's logic level
    (p2kb architecture/smart_pins.yaml in_signal_semantics.when_smart_pin_mode
    _is_OFF), so the streamer's input bit for P3 reads the driven 0. Checked
    in-run by TESTP at every block. P0 is named by the non-Goertzel mode's
    pin field, but that mode's output enable (D[23]) is 0 and its data is 0.
    No DAC is enabled anywhere (Goertzel D[27:24] = 0, imm-mode D[27:24] = 0).
    _clkfreq = 200 MHz. Run time well under 10 ms of engine time.

  DEBUGGER CONFOUND (EF-057): DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001. All streamer work and
  every GETXACC runs in a dedicated PASM cog started by COGINIT from DAT; cog 0
  (Spin2) only waits on the hub mailbox and prints.

  CONSTRUCTION (brief Part 2 "constructing a burst")
    NCO frequency $8000_0000 (SETXFRQ once, thousands of clocks before any
      XINIT; no SETQ ever precedes an XINIT).
    Goertzel D = $F007_0000 | count: mode bits [15:12]=1111, [11:8]=0000 (no
      DAC), [7]=0 (sinc1: xterm REPLACED each clock), [6:3]=0000 (pins 0..3),
      [2:0]=111.
    S_ON   = $0008_80A5: imm[19]=1 (invert P3), imm[15]=1 (sum P3 only),
             imm[14:12]=0, imm[11:9]=000, imm[8:0]=$0A5 (LUT address).
    S_ZERO = $0008_00A5: imm[15:12]=0 -> every term zero (the "zero burst").
    LUT long $173D_0000 written to ALL 512 LUT longs once, before the first
      burst, then read back (control). bits[23:16] = $3D = 61 = g (cosine,
      feeds X); bits[31:24] = $17 = 23 (sine, feeds Y -- NOT traced by the
      brief, Y is informational only).
    P3 low, imm[19]=1  -> bit differs from imm[19] -> term = +g -> C = +61.
    P3 high (CAL only) -> bit matches imm[19]      -> term = -g -> C = -61.

  RUN ORDER (one engine cog, all of it)
    CAL      preamble + 64-count burst with P3 LOW, then again with P3 HIGH,
             then P3 back LOW for the rest. Control: both deltas whole
             multiples of 61, low one positive, high one its exact negative
             -> proves C = +61 comes from P3 through the constructed term.
    x8 reps, each:
      phase (i)  Half A: preamble -> B; G1 idle; XINIT $4000_0400 (1-pin imm
                 mode, output off, count $0400) and G2 as the NEXT instruction;
                 G2L ~100 clocks into that imm burst (XFI must still be 0);
                 wait idle; G3.
      run A      preamble -> B; P idle read; Goertzel burst N=256, no read;
                 wait idle; RA.  dA = RA - P.
      run B      preamble -> B; P idle read; same burst; WAITX dly; R1 mid
                 burst (XFI must still be 0); wait idle; R2.
                 dB = R1 + R2 - P.  Scored only if (R1-P) is a whole
                 multiple of C with 1 <= k1 < kA (read landed inside).
      dly schedule (WAITX operand): 30,30,30,30 (= brief's ~32 clocks, four
      repeats) then 62,94,126,190 (sampling plan: the read point moves, the
      verdict must not).
    Preamble = (a) charge burst count 8 S_ON, wait idle; (b) zero burst count
      4 S_ZERO, wait idle; (c) GETXACC -> B.  Retried up to 3x if B = 0.
    "Wait idle" = WAITX 4000 (> count + 16 for every burst, incl. $0400),
      then POLLXFI must report the streamer finished (control).

  WHY P AS THE HALF-B BASELINE (improvement on the brief): the brief uses B.
  P is one more idle GETXACC immediately before the XINIT. If Half A holds,
  P = B exactly (and P-B is scored as more Half A evidence). If Half A is
  wrong (idle clear works), B's own read zeroed xsum and P reads that 0 --
  so P is the true starting xsum in BOTH worlds and Half B's arithmetic does
  not silently inherit a Half A failure.

  EXPECTED VALUES IF THE PREDICTION IS TRUE
    CAL: kLO = +k, kHI = -k, k near 64 (my derivation: N-1 = 63; first-term
         timing is `inferred` in the brief, so gated only to 56..72).
    Half A: every G1, G2, G2L, G3, P equals its B exactly -> 50/50 zero diffs.
    Half B: dA = kA*61 with kA near 256 (gated 248..264), identical every rep;
            k1 grows 1:1 with dly; dd = 0 in every scored rep.

  IN-RUN CONTROLS (any failure prints "RIG FAIL: ..." and withholds verdicts)
    LUT readback 512/512; P3 level at every block; XFI finished after every
    wait-idle and NOT finished at every mid-burst read; every preamble B <> 0
    (gates Half A); CAL sign/multiple/negation (gates both); every dA a whole
    positive multiple of C inside 248..264 (gates Half B).

  VERIFIED ENCODINGS (pnut-ts v1.55.8, `pnut-ts -d -l`, decoded from the .lst
  object hex dump; engine at object offset $032 = cog $000):
    GETXACC b_   $FD61C41E   [27:21]=1101011 [20:18]=000 [8:0]=000011110
    GETXACC p_   $FD61C81E   GETXACC g1_ $FD61D01E   GETXACC g2_ $FD61D41E
    GETXACC g2l_ $FD61D81E   GETXACC r1_ $FD61E01E   (each followed by
                              MOV x,0-0 = $F601xx00, S field 0, takes Y)
    XINIT dch_,son_     $FCA184C7   [27:19]=110010100, L=I=0, D=$0C2 S=$0C7
    XINIT dzero_,szero_ $FCA186C8   D=$0C3 S=$0C8
    XINIT dcal_,son_    $FCA188C7   D=$0C4 S=$0C7
    XINIT drun_,son_    $FCA18AC7   D=$0C5 S=$0C7
    XINIT dimm_,simm_   $FCA18CC9   D=$0C6 S=$0C9; next word = GETXACC g2_
    SETXFRQ frq_        $FD61961D   [8:0]=000011101, D=$0CB (frq_), L=0
    WRLUT lutv_,z_      $FC3194E1   [27:20]=11000011, D=$0CA S=$0E1
    SETLUTS #0 $FD640037 | WRPIN #0,#3 $FC0C0003 | DRVL #3 $FD640658
    DRVH #3 $FD640659 | TESTP #3 WC $FD740640 | POLLXFI WC $FD701624
    WAITX dly_ $FD61BE1F (register) | ALTS rep_,#dlytab $F995B6CC
    WAITX ##4000 = AUGD $FF800007 + $FD67401F -> (7<<9)|$1A0 = 4000
    DAT data longs, byte-for-byte from the dump:
    dch_  = $F007_0008   dzero_ = $F007_0004   dcal_ = $F007_0040
    drun_ = $F007_0100   dimm_  = $4000_0400   son_  = $0008_80A5
    szero_= $0008_00A5   simm_  = $0000_0000   lutv_ = $173D_0000
    frq_  = $8000_0000   dlytab = 30,30,30,30,62,94,126,190
    Goertzel mode bits (D[31:16] = $F007): [15:12]=1111 [11:8]=0000 (no DAC)
      [7]=0 (sinc1) [6:3]=0000 (group 0, pins 0..3) [2:0]=111.
    Non-Goertzel (D[31:16] = $4000): [15:12]=0100 [11:8]=0000 [7]=0 (%e off).
    son_: bit19=1 bit15=1 bits14:12=000 bits11:9=000 bits8:0=$0A5.
    szero_: bit19=1 bits15:12=0000 bits8:0=$0A5.

  DEPENDS ON CLAIMS THE BRIEF MARKS inferred / undetermined
    - first term of a burst (LUT read latency): inferred. Protected: every
      LUT long is identical, and all comparisons are between identically
      constructed bursts (dA vs dB; CAL lo vs hi), so a stale first term
      cancels. Only the absolute k is affected, and it is only range-gated.
    - what the pin input bus carries / what a floating pin reads:
      undetermined. Protected: P3 is driven, never floating; TESTP checks it;
      CAL proves the term follows P3 (sign flip); every delta must be a whole
      multiple of 61.
    - XINIT-to-first-active-clock and GETXACC pipeline length: undetermined.
      Protected: no prediction of the landing clock; the landing is checked
      from R1 itself (brief Part 5) and by XFI still 0 after the read.
    - Part 4 "zero burst with a read inside leaves both zero": inferred, NOT
      used.

  HOW TO RUN: load with pnut-term-ts (or PNut) with DEBUG enabled, i.e. a
  `pnut-ts -d` build (without -d every debug() is dropped and a clean compile
  is a false pass). Output ends with "@@@ TEST COMPLETE @@@". The verdict
  lines are "VERDICT HALF A: ..." and "VERDICT HALF B: ...".

  Build: pnut-ts -d -l test-so80-getxacc-clear-gating.spin2
}

CON  ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq   = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001                 ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  PIN        = 3                          ' 4g+3, g = 0
  G_COS      = 61                         ' LUT bits[23:16] -> C for X
  G_SIN      = 23                         ' LUT bits[31:24] -> Y (informational)
  LUTADDR    = $0A5
  LUTVAL     = (G_SIN << 24) | (G_COS << 16)

  MODE_G     = $F007_0000                 ' Goertzel sinc1, no DAC, pins 0..3
  N_CHARGE   = 8
  N_ZERO     = 4
  N_CAL      = 64
  N_RUN      = 256
  S_ON       = (1 << 19) | (1 << 15) | LUTADDR
  S_ZERO     = (1 << 19) | LUTADDR
  D_IMM      = $4000_0400                 ' 1-pin immediate, D[23]=0, no DAC, count $400
  FRQ        = $8000_0000
  WAIT_IDLE  = 4000                       ' > $0400 + 16
  G2L_WAIT   = 100
  REPS       = 8
  MAXTRY     = 3
  K_TOL      = 8

  ' mailbox layout (longs)
  CAL_LO     = 0
  CAL_HI     = 7
  CAL_REC    = 7                          ' fields per CAL record (CB..CT)
  CB = 0, CBY = 1, CP = 2, CPY = 3, CR = 4, CRY = 5, CT = 6
  REP0       = 14
  REC        = 28
  O_B1 = 0, O_B1Y = 1, O_G1 = 2, O_G1Y = 3, O_G2 = 4, O_G2Y = 5
  O_G2L = 6, O_G2LY = 7, O_G3 = 8, O_G3Y = 9, O_T1 = 10
  O_BA = 11, O_BAY = 12, O_PA = 13, O_PAY = 14, O_RA = 15, O_RAY = 16, O_TA = 17
  O_BB = 18, O_BBY = 19, O_PB = 20, O_PBY = 21, O_R1 = 22, O_R1Y = 23
  O_R2 = 24, O_R2Y = 25, O_DLY = 26, O_TB = 27
  CTRL       = REP0 + REPS * REC
  C_XFIF = 0, C_XFIL = 1, C_PINF = 2, C_PINL = 3, C_LUTF = 4, C_DONE = 5
  MBLEN      = CTRL + 8

VAR  ' ---- Mailbox & Scoring State ----
  long mb[MBLEN]
  long rigA, rigB, klo
  long nObs, nMoved, nZeroed, nMovedImm
  long cls[10], nScored

PUB main() | cogn, t0
'' Run the SO80 rig: launch the engine cog, wait for it, then print raw data,
'' controls, and both verdicts.
''

  longfill(@mb, 0, MBLEN)
  debug("=== SO80: GETXACC clear gating (Half A) + held-term residue (Half B) ===")
  debug("rig: NO jumper; engine cog drives P3 low; clk 200 MHz; reps ", udec_(REPS))
  cogn := coginit(NEWCOG, @engine, @mb)
  t0 := getct()
  repeat until mb[CTRL + C_DONE] == 1 or (getct() - t0) > clkfreq * 2
  if mb[CTRL + C_DONE] <> 1
    debug("RIG FAIL: engine done flag: expected 1, got ", sdec_(mb[CTRL + C_DONE]), " -- no verdicts")
    cogstop(cogn)
    finish()
  show_raw()
  controls()
  half_a()
  half_b()
  info_y()
  debug("@@@ TEST COMPLETE @@@")
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat


PRI at(repIdx, fieldOffset) : fieldVal
' Read one field from a rep record in the mailbox.
'
' @param repIdx - Rep index (0..REPS-1)
' @param fieldOffset - Field offset within one rep record (an O_* constant)
' @returns fieldVal - The mailbox long at that rep/field location

  fieldVal := mb[REP0 + repIdx * REC + fieldOffset]


PRI fail_both()
' Mark both Half A and Half B verdicts as rig-failed (a shared control tripped).

  rigA := TRUE
  rigB := TRUE


' ---------------------------------------------------------------- raw data --
PRI show_raw() | repIdx, calSide
' Print every raw mailbox field before any interpretation, for hand audit.

  debug("--- RAW (X = cos accumulator, Y = sin accumulator; all SIGNED) ---")
  repeat calSide from 0 to 1
    debug("CAL pin ", zstr_(calSide ? @s_hi : @s_lo), ": B=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CB]), " P=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CP]), " R=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CR]), "  Y: B=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CBY]), " P=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CPY]), " R=", sdec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CRY]), " tries=", udec_(mb[calSide*CAL_REC+CT]))
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), " (i)  B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_B1)), " G1=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G1)), " G2=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2)), " G2L=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2L)), " G3=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G3)), " tries=", udec_(at(repIdx,O_T1)))
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), " (i)Y B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_B1Y)), " G1=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G1Y)), " G2=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2Y)), " G2L=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2LY)), " G3=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G3Y)))
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), " runA B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_BA)), " P=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PA)), " RA=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_RA)), "  Y: B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_BAY)), " P=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PAY)), " RA=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_RAY)), " tries=", udec_(at(repIdx,O_TA)))
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), " runB B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_BB)), " P=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PB)), " R1=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_R1)), " R2=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_R2)), " waitx=", udec_(at(repIdx,O_DLY)), " tries=", udec_(at(repIdx,O_TB)))
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), " runBY B=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_BBY)), " P=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PBY)), " R1=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_R1Y)), " R2=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_R2Y)))


' ------------------------------------------------------- in-run controls --
PRI controls() | ctrlVal, repIdx, dlo, dhi, khi, badCount
' Check every in-run control the engine recorded and set rigA/rigB on failure.

  rigA := FALSE
  rigB := FALSE
  debug("--- IN-RUN CONTROLS ---")
  ctrlVal := mb[CTRL + C_LUTF]
  if ctrlVal <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: LUT readback: expected 0 mismatches of 512, got ", udec_(ctrlVal))
    fail_both()
  ctrlVal := mb[CTRL + C_XFIF]
  if ctrlVal <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: streamer XFI (finished) flag wrong ", udec_(ctrlVal), " times; last at site ", udec_(mb[CTRL + C_XFIL]), " (expected finished after each wait-idle, running at each mid-burst read)")
    fail_both()
  ctrlVal := mb[CTRL + C_PINF]
  if ctrlVal <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: P3 level wrong ", udec_(ctrlVal), " times; last at site ", udec_(mb[CTRL + C_PINL]), " (expected the driven level)")
    fail_both()

  ' every preamble B must be nonzero, or a clear that wrongly reached xsum
  ' would be invisible (brief Part 5 preamble)
  badCount := 0
  repeat ctrlVal from 0 to 1
    if mb[ctrlVal*CAL_REC + CB] == 0
      badCount++
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    if at(repIdx,O_B1) == 0 or at(repIdx,O_BA) == 0 or at(repIdx,O_BB) == 0
      badCount++
  if badCount
    debug("RIG FAIL: preamble B = 0 after ", udec_(MAXTRY), " tries in ", udec_(badCount), " place(s): expected nonzero (gates Half A)")
    rigA := TRUE

  ' CAL: the term must follow P3 and be exactly +-61 per active clock
  dlo := mb[CAL_LO + CR] - mb[CAL_LO + CP]
  dhi := mb[CAL_HI + CR] - mb[CAL_HI + CP]
  debug("CAL: dLO=", sdec_(dlo), " dHI=", sdec_(dhi), "  (expect dLO = +k*61, dHI = -k*61, k in ", udec_(N_CAL - K_TOL), "..", udec_(N_CAL + K_TOL), ")")
  if (dlo // G_COS) <> 0 or (dhi // G_COS) <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: CAL deltas not whole multiples of g=61: dLO=", sdec_(dlo), " dHI=", sdec_(dhi))
    fail_both()
  else
    klo := dlo / G_COS
    khi := dhi / G_COS
    debug("CAL: kLO=", sdec_(klo), " kHI=", sdec_(khi), "  (my derivation N-1 = ", udec_(N_CAL - 1), "; first term is inferred)")
    if klo < N_CAL - K_TOL or klo > N_CAL + K_TOL
      debug("RIG FAIL: CAL pin-LOW k: expected ", udec_(N_CAL - K_TOL), "..", udec_(N_CAL + K_TOL), ", got ", sdec_(klo))
      fail_both()
    if khi <> -klo
      debug("RIG FAIL: CAL pin-HIGH k must be the exact negative: expected ", sdec_(-klo), ", got ", sdec_(khi))
      fail_both()

  ' Half B construction: every dA a whole positive multiple of C, k near N
  badCount := 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    ctrlVal := at(repIdx,O_RA) - at(repIdx,O_PA)
    if (ctrlVal // G_COS) <> 0 or ctrlVal / G_COS < N_RUN - K_TOL or ctrlVal / G_COS > N_RUN + K_TOL
      debug("RIG FAIL: rep ", udec_(repIdx), " dA=", sdec_(ctrlVal), ": expected k*61 with k in ", udec_(N_RUN - K_TOL), "..", udec_(N_RUN + K_TOL), " (C not constant / burst not as constructed)")
      badCount++
  if badCount
    rigB := TRUE
  if not rigA and not rigB
    debug("controls: all passed (LUT, XFI, P3 level, B<>0, CAL sign+negation, dA)")


' ------------------------------------------------------------------ Half A --
PRI half_a() | repIdx, calSide
' Tally every idle/non-Goertzel GETXACC read against its preamble B and print
' the Half A verdict.

  nObs := 0
  nMoved := 0
  nZeroed := 0
  nMovedImm := 0
  debug("--- HALF A: idle / non-Goertzel reads vs preamble B (TRUE: every d = 0; FALSE: d <> 0, d = -B means cleared) ---")
  repeat calSide from 0 to 1
    tallyA(mb[calSide*CAL_REC + CP], mb[calSide*CAL_REC + CB], FALSE)
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_G1),  at(repIdx,O_B1), FALSE)
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_G2),  at(repIdx,O_B1), TRUE)
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_G2L), at(repIdx,O_B1), TRUE)
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_G3),  at(repIdx,O_B1), FALSE)
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_PA),  at(repIdx,O_BA), FALSE)
    tallyA(at(repIdx,O_PB),  at(repIdx,O_BB), FALSE)
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), ": dG1=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G1)-at(repIdx,O_B1)), " dG2=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2)-at(repIdx,O_B1)), " dG2L=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G2L)-at(repIdx,O_B1)), " dG3=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_G3)-at(repIdx,O_B1)), " dPA=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PA)-at(repIdx,O_BA)), " dPB=", sdec_(at(repIdx,O_PB)-at(repIdx,O_BB)))
  debug("Half A: ", udec_(nObs), " reads; moved ", udec_(nMoved), " (non-Goertzel-active ", udec_(nMovedImm), "); read exactly 0 ", udec_(nZeroed))
  if rigA
    debug("VERDICT HALF A: NO VERDICT -- RIG FAIL above")
  elseif nMoved == 0
    debug("VERDICT HALF A: CONFIRMED -- all ", udec_(nObs), " idle/non-Goertzel GETXACC reads equal their B bit-for-bit")
  elseif nZeroed
    debug("VERDICT HALF A: REFUTED -- ", udec_(nZeroed), " read(s) returned 0 (d = -B): the clear reached xsum idle/outside Goertzel; ", udec_(nMoved), " moved in all")
  else
    debug("VERDICT HALF A: REFUTED -- ", udec_(nMoved), " read(s) differ from B (not zero): xsum moved while idle/outside Goertzel")


PRI tallyA(readVal, baselineVal, bImm)
' Count one Half A observation: did the GETXACC read move away from baseline?
'
' @param readVal - The GETXACC (or idle) reading being scored
' @param baselineVal - The preamble B this reading is compared against
' @param bImm - TRUE when this read is inside a non-Goertzel-active burst

  nObs++
  if readVal <> baselineVal
    nMoved++
    if bImm
      nMovedImm++
    if readVal == 0
      nZeroed++


' ------------------------------------------------------------------ Half B --
' class: 0 confirmed, 1 dd=R1, 2 dd=-C, 3 dd=+C, 4 other multiple,
'        5 not a multiple (inconclusive), 9 unscored (read not inside burst)
PRI half_b() | repIdx, termC, dA, kA, baselineP, k1, dB, dd, classCode
' Score every rep's mid-burst read against its no-read counterpart and print
' the Half B verdict.

  longfill(@cls, 0, 10)
  nScored := 0
  termC := G_COS                           ' C = +61 with P3 low (CAL-checked)
  debug("--- HALF B: dd = dB - dA (TRUE: 0; FALSE: R1 | -C | +C | other multiple of C) ---")
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    baselineP := at(repIdx,O_PB)
    dA := at(repIdx,O_RA) - at(repIdx,O_PA)
    kA := dA / termC
    dB := at(repIdx,O_R1) + at(repIdx,O_R2) - baselineP
    dd := dB - dA
    if ((at(repIdx,O_R1) - baselineP) // termC) <> 0
      classCode := 9
      k1 := 0
    else
      k1 := (at(repIdx,O_R1) - baselineP) / termC
      if k1 < 1 or k1 >= kA
        classCode := 9
      elseif dd == 0
        classCode := 0
      elseif dd == at(repIdx,O_R1)
        classCode := 1
      elseif dd == -termC
        classCode := 2
      elseif dd == termC
        classCode := 3
      elseif (dd // termC) == 0
        classCode := 4
      else
        classCode := 5
    cls[classCode]++
    if classCode <> 9
      nScored++
    debug("rep ", udec_(repIdx), ": waitx=", udec_(at(repIdx,O_DLY)), " kA=", sdec_(kA), " k1=", sdec_(k1), " k1-waitx=", sdec_(k1 - at(repIdx,O_DLY)), " dA=", sdec_(dA), " dB=", sdec_(dB), " dd=", sdec_(dd), " class=", udec_(classCode))
  debug("classes: 0 conf=", udec_(cls[0]), " 1 dd=R1=", udec_(cls[1]), " 2 dd=-C=", udec_(cls[2]), " 3 dd=+C=", udec_(cls[3]), " 4 other=", udec_(cls[4]), " 5 non-multiple=", udec_(cls[5]), " 9 unscored=", udec_(cls[9]))
  debug("(k1-waitx should be the same number in every scored rep: the read point is deterministic)")
  if rigB
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: NO VERDICT -- RIG FAIL above")
  elseif nScored < 4
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: INCONCLUSIVE -- only ", udec_(nScored), " of ", udec_(REPS), " mid-burst reads landed inside the burst (need 4); move the read")
  elseif cls[5]
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: INCONCLUSIVE -- dd not a whole multiple of C in ", udec_(cls[5]), " rep(s): the Part 2 construction did not hold")
  elseif cls[0] == nScored
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: CONFIRMED -- dd = 0 in all ", udec_(nScored), " scored reps: the mid-burst read leaves exactly the held term")
  elseif cls[1] == nScored
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: REFUTED -- dd = R1 in all scored reps: GETXACC did not clear xsum even while the Goertzel streamer ran")
  elseif cls[2] == nScored
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: REFUTED -- dd = -C in all scored reps: the clear left a TRUE zero (held term lost)")
  elseif cls[3] == nScored
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: REFUTED -- dd = +C in all scored reps: the held term was counted twice")
  elseif cls[4] == nScored
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: REFUTED -- dd a nonzero multiple of C other than R1/-C/+C in all scored reps (see dd above)")
  else
    debug("VERDICT HALF B: INCONCLUSIVE -- mixed classes across scored reps (see class counts); the result did not repeat")


' -------------------------------------------- Y channel, informational only --
PRI info_y() | repIdx, dlo, dhi, dA, dB, moved
' Print the Y (sine) channel deltas alongside X, for the record only -- the
' brief does not trace Y and no verdict is scored on it.

  debug("--- Y (sine, LUT bits[31:24]=23) -- INFORMATIONAL, not traced by the brief ---")
  dlo := mb[CAL_LO + CRY] - mb[CAL_LO + CPY]
  dhi := mb[CAL_HI + CRY] - mb[CAL_HI + CPY]
  debug("Y CAL: dLO=", sdec_(dlo), " dHI=", sdec_(dhi), " (as X, expect +-k*23)")
  moved := 0
  repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
    if at(repIdx,O_G1Y) <> at(repIdx,O_B1Y) or at(repIdx,O_G2Y) <> at(repIdx,O_B1Y) or at(repIdx,O_G2LY) <> at(repIdx,O_B1Y) or at(repIdx,O_G3Y) <> at(repIdx,O_B1Y)
      moved++
    if at(repIdx,O_PAY) <> at(repIdx,O_BAY) or at(repIdx,O_PBY) <> at(repIdx,O_BBY)
      moved++
    dA := at(repIdx,O_RAY) - at(repIdx,O_PAY)
    dB := at(repIdx,O_R1Y) + at(repIdx,O_R2Y) - at(repIdx,O_PBY)
    debug("Y rep ", udec_(repIdx), ": dA=", sdec_(dA), " dB=", sdec_(dB), " dd=", sdec_(dB - dA))
  debug("Y Half-A-style checks that moved: ", udec_(moved), " (0 expected if ysum behaves as xsum)")


DAT  ' ---- CAL Label Strings ----
s_lo            byte    "LOW ", 0
s_hi            byte    "HIGH", 0

' ===========================================================================
'  ENGINE -- the only cog that touches the streamer or GETXACC
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Streamer Engine Cog ----
engine
                mov     mbase_, ptra
                setluts #0                      ' LUT sharing OFF, explicitly
                wrpin   #0, #PIN                ' P3: smart pin off, reset config
                drvl    #PIN                    ' P3 plain output, driven low
                mov     pinexp_, #0
                setxfrq frq_                    ' NCO frequency $8000_0000

                mov     z_, #$1FF               ' same long in every LUT entry
.fill           wrlut   lutv_, z_
                djnf    z_, #.fill
                mov     z_, #$1FF               ' control: read all 512 back
.chk            rdlut   t_, z_
                cmp     t_, lutv_               wz
        if_nz   add     lutfail_, #1
                djnf    z_, #.chk
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE             ' pin settles; SETXFRQ long past

' ---- CAL: P3 low, then P3 high, then back low ------------------------------
                mov     ptra, mbase_            ' CAL_LO record
                mov     site_, #1
                call    #pin_check
                call    #preamble
                getxacc p_
                mov     py_, 0-0
                xinit   dcal_, son_
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #2
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc r_
                mov     ry_, 0-0
                call    #put_cal

                drvh    #PIN                    ' CAL_HI record follows
                mov     pinexp_, #1
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #3
                call    #pin_check
                call    #preamble
                getxacc p_
                mov     py_, 0-0
                xinit   dcal_, son_
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #4
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc r_
                mov     ry_, 0-0
                call    #put_cal

                drvl    #PIN                    ' P3 low for everything below
                mov     pinexp_, #0
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #5
                call    #pin_check

' ---- repetitions -------------------------------------------------------------
                mov     rep_, #0
                mov     recp_, mbase_
                add     recp_, ##REP0 * 4
rep_loop        mov     ptra, recp_

                ' -- phase (i): Half A, mode gating --
                mov     site_, #10
                call    #pin_check
                call    #preamble
                getxacc g1_                     ' G1: idle
                mov     g1y_, 0-0
                xinit   dimm_, simm_            ' non-Goertzel mode, drives nothing
                getxacc g2_                     ' G2: the very next instruction
                mov     g2y_, 0-0
                waitx   #G2L_WAIT
                getxacc g2l_                    ' G2L: well inside the imm burst
                mov     g2ly_, 0-0
                mov     site_, #11
                call    #xfi_mid                ' imm streamer must still be running
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #12
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc g3_                     ' G3: idle again
                mov     g3y_, 0-0
                wrlong  b_, ptra++
                wrlong  by_, ptra++
                wrlong  g1_, ptra++
                wrlong  g1y_, ptra++
                wrlong  g2_, ptra++
                wrlong  g2y_, ptra++
                wrlong  g2l_, ptra++
                wrlong  g2ly_, ptra++
                wrlong  g3_, ptra++
                wrlong  g3y_, ptra++
                wrlong  tries_, ptra++

                ' -- run A: burst N, no read inside --
                mov     site_, #20
                call    #pin_check
                call    #preamble
                getxacc p_                      ' P: last idle read before XINIT
                mov     py_, 0-0
                xinit   drun_, son_
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #21
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc r_                      ' RA
                mov     ry_, 0-0
                wrlong  b_, ptra++
                wrlong  by_, ptra++
                wrlong  p_, ptra++
                wrlong  py_, ptra++
                wrlong  r_, ptra++
                wrlong  ry_, ptra++
                wrlong  tries_, ptra++

                ' -- run B: same burst, one GETXACC inside it --
                mov     site_, #30
                call    #pin_check
                alts    rep_, #dlytab
                mov     dly_, 0-0               ' delay chosen BEFORE the burst
                call    #preamble
                getxacc p_
                mov     py_, 0-0
                xinit   drun_, son_
                waitx   dly_
                getxacc r1_                     ' R1: mid-burst
                mov     r1y_, 0-0
                mov     site_, #31
                call    #xfi_mid                ' streamer must still be running
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                mov     site_, #32
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc r2_                     ' R2: after idle
                mov     r2y_, 0-0
                wrlong  b_, ptra++
                wrlong  by_, ptra++
                wrlong  p_, ptra++
                wrlong  py_, ptra++
                wrlong  r1_, ptra++
                wrlong  r1y_, ptra++
                wrlong  r2_, ptra++
                wrlong  r2y_, ptra++
                wrlong  dly_, ptra++
                wrlong  tries_, ptra++
                mov     site_, #33
                call    #pin_check

                add     recp_, ##REC * 4
                add     rep_, #1
                cmp     rep_, #REPS             wz
        if_nz   jmp     #rep_loop

' ---- controls, then done (done is always the last hub write) ----------------
                mov     site_, #99
                call    #pin_check
                mov     ptra, mbase_
                add     ptra, ##CTRL * 4
                wrlong  xfifail_, ptra++
                wrlong  xfilast_, ptra++
                wrlong  pinfail_, ptra++
                wrlong  pinlast_, ptra++
                wrlong  lutfail_, ptra++
                wrlong  #1, ptra                ' C_DONE
                cogid   t_
                cogstop t_

' ---- preamble: charge burst, zero burst, read B (retry while B = 0) --------
preamble
                mov     tries_, #0
.again          add     tries_, #1
                xinit   dch_, son_              ' (a) charge: count 8, imm[15] set
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                call    #xfi_end
                xinit   dzero_, szero_          ' (b) zero: count 4, imm[15:12] = 0
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                call    #xfi_end
                getxacc b_                      ' (c) B
                mov     by_, 0-0
                tjnz    b_, #.done
                cmp     tries_, #MAXTRY         wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.again
.done           ret

put_cal
                wrlong  b_, ptra++
                wrlong  by_, ptra++
                wrlong  p_, ptra++
                wrlong  py_, ptra++
                wrlong  r_, ptra++
                wrlong  ry_, ptra++
                wrlong  tries_, ptra++
                ret

' expect the streamer FINISHED (XFI set) -- after a wait-idle
xfi_end
                pollxfi                         wc
        if_nc   add     xfifail_, #1
        if_nc   mov     xfilast_, site_
                ret

' expect the streamer still RUNNING (XFI clear) -- right after a mid-burst read
xfi_mid
                pollxfi                         wc
        if_c    add     xfifail_, #1
        if_c    mov     xfilast_, site_
                ret

' expect P3 at the driven level
pin_check
                testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     t_
                cmp     t_, pinexp_             wz
        if_nz   add     pinfail_, #1
        if_nz   mov     pinlast_, site_
                ret

' ---- constants (verified in the .lst) ----------------------------------------
dch_            long    MODE_G | N_CHARGE
dzero_          long    MODE_G | N_ZERO
dcal_           long    MODE_G | N_CAL
drun_           long    MODE_G | N_RUN
dimm_           long    D_IMM
son_            long    S_ON
szero_          long    S_ZERO
simm_           long    0
lutv_           long    LUTVAL
frq_            long    FRQ
dlytab          long    30, 30, 30, 30, 62, 94, 126, 190

' ---- counters: initialised to 0 by the COGINIT load (long, not res) --------
xfifail_        long    0
xfilast_        long    0
pinfail_        long    0
pinlast_        long    0
lutfail_        long    0

mbase_          res     1
recp_           res     1
rep_            res     1
site_           res     1
pinexp_         res     1
tries_          res     1
dly_            res     1
t_              res     1
z_              res     1
b_              res     1
by_             res     1
p_              res     1
py_             res     1
r_              res     1
ry_             res     1
g1_             res     1
g1y_            res     1
g2_             res     1
g2y_            res     1
g2l_            res     1
g2ly_           res     1
g3_             res     1
g3y_            res     1
r1_             res     1
r1y_            res     1
r2_             res     1
r2y_            res     1

